" cy=\"50.64573991031392\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(52%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nijmegen the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.41) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.12).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'>0.115</td><td class='num'>16.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'>0.128</td><td class='num'>14.9%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.273</td><td class='num'>14.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.406</td><td class='num'>11.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.8425,"lon":5.85278,"n":737,"n_cities":213,"name":"Nijmegen","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003441860465116279,"n":215,"obs":0.15348837209302327,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.080253164556962,"n":79,"obs":0.3670886075949367,"sig":true},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.2,"mean":